# Agent Rules - Execution and Skill Rules

## 1. Rule Loading
- At the start of every session, you MUST read and follow the instructions in [antigravity/antigravity_rules.md](file:///d:/GitHub/MySkills/antigravity/antigravity_rules.md).

## 2. Skill Execution Constraint
- Whenever the user initiates a task that matches the description or keywords of a skill in [antigravity/.agents/skills/](file:///d:/GitHub/MySkills/antigravity/.agents/skills/) (such as `srs-workflow`, `srs-generator`, `team`, `team-ba` etc.):
  - You MUST load the corresponding `SKILL.md` file.
  - You MUST execute the skill's pipeline strictly step-by-step (from Phase 0 to Phase N).
  - You MUST NOT skip any brainstorm gates, option gates, user review gates, validation commands, or success criteria checks.
  - For each phase, you must wait for user confirmation or inputs where requested.

## 3. Sub-Agent Checklist Compliance
- When acting as a specific sub-agent (e.g. planner, tester, code-reviewer, git-manager), you MUST load the corresponding markdown definition file from [antigravity/.agents/](file:///d:/GitHub/MySkills/antigravity/.agents/) and apply its checklist and guidelines in full.

## 4. Planning Mode & Approval Gate
- For any non-trivial changes, you MUST write or update `implementation_plan.md` in the brain directory, set `request_feedback` to `true` in metadata, and immediately STOP calling tools.
- Do NOT proceed to write code or run modifying commands until the user gives explicit approval.
